[209.988592, "o", "\u001b[0m← \u001b[0mEdit my_website/public/blog/scaling-graph-neural-networks.html\r\nIndex: my_website/public/blog/scaling-graph-neural-networks.html\r\n===================================================================\r\n--- my_website/public/blog/scaling-graph-neural-networks.html\r\n+++ my_website/public/blog/scaling-graph-neural-networks.html\r\n@@ -105,15 +105,13 @@\r\n             leakage from overlapping neighborhoods and lets us measure how performance decays\r\n             as we move away from the training region. A model that generalizes across a volume\r\n             boundary is more convincing than one that generalizes across a random edge split.\r\n           </p>\r\n-          <div class=\"prose\">\r\n-            <pre><code># Sketch: stratified neighborhood sampling\r\n+          <pre><code># Sketch: stratified neighborhood sampling\r\n for batch in regions:\r\n     nodes = sample_by_morphology(batch, strata)\r\n     subgraph = k_hop_neighbors(nodes, k=2, edge_types=all)\r\n     loss = model(subgraph, targets[nodes])</code></pre>\r\n-          </div>\r\n \r\n           <h2 id=\"evaluation\">Evaluate the motif, not just the label</h2>\r\n           <p>\r\n             Synapse classification accuracy is a useful number, but connectivity inference is\r\n\r\n"]
